" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{7\\text{i}t},$ where $t,s\\in R?$$\\,L(f(t))=$\n{{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{7\\text{i}t},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{e}^{7\\text{i}t}\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(7\\text{i}-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating in the usual way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(7\\text{i}-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(7\\text{i}-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{7\\text{i}-s}{e}^{(7\\text{i}-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7\\text{i}-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7\\text{i}-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(7\\text{i}-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}\\cdot {e}^{7\\text{i}a}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall Euler's formula:\n\n$$\n{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}[{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7a)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7a))].\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following cases:\n\n- For $s<0,$ the term ${e}^{-sa}$ increases without bound while $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7a)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7a)$ oscillates rapidly as $a\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the limit does not exist for $s<0.$\n\n- For $s=0,$ we have simply $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7a)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7a),$ which oscillates rapidly as $a\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the limit does not exist for $s=0.$\n\n- For $s>0,$ the term ${e}^{-sa}$ decays to zero while $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7a)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7a)$ oscillates rapidly as $a\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the limit of their product equals zero.\n\nTherefore, for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}[{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7a)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7a))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of ${e}^{7\\text{i}t}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}},$ defined for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0b570eda3f9b59381be1afdf44aa0f5f11c8c6a23ee6730025f33449cb24786"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{s+7\\text{i}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{s+7\\text{i}}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{s-7\\text{i}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{s-7\\text{i}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "s<0"] ["math" "s>-7"] ["math" "s>0"] ["math" "s>7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340737" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "s>0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{-3\\text{i}t/8},$ where $t,s\\in R?$$\\,L(f(t))=$\n{{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the function $f(t)={e}^{-3\\text{i}t/8},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{e}^{-3\\text{i}t/8}\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-3\\text{i}/8-s)t}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating in the usual way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{(-3\\text{i}/8-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{a}{e}^{(-3\\text{i}/8-s)t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{-3\\text{i}/8-s}{e}^{(-3\\text{i}/8-s)t})|}_{0}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3\\text{i}/8-s}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-3\\text{i}/8-s)a}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}(1-{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{(-3\\text{i}/8-s)a}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}-\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}\\cdot {e}^{-3\\text{i}a/8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall Euler's formula:\n\n$$\n{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta }=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}-\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}[{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3a/8)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3a/8))].\n$$\n\nNow, we have the following cases:\n\n- For $s<0,$ the term ${e}^{-sa}$ increases without bound while $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3a/8)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3a/8)$ oscillates rapidly as $a\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the limit does not exist for $s<0.$\n\n- For $s=0,$ we have simply $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3a/8)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3a/8),$ which oscillates rapidly as $a\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the limit does not exist for $s=0.$\n\n- For $s>0,$ the term ${e}^{-sa}$ decays to zero while $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3a/8)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3a/8)$ oscillates rapidly as $a\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the limit of their product equals zero.\n\nTherefore, for $s>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & =\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}-\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}[{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{e}^{-sa}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3a/8)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3a/8))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}/8} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{8s+3\\text{i}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Laplace transform of ${e}^{-3\\text{i}t/8}$ is $F(s)=\\frac{8}{8s+3\\text{i}},$ defined for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340748" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d0b570eda3f9b59381be1afdf44aa0f5f11c8c6a23ee6730025f33449cb24786"} {"question" "q-340748" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042893/state.json" "file_sha256" "caddfd3715359a191831784912dca6bce792c61a21c4f35b5027000a8e5305cd"} {"question" "q-340748" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3s+8\\text{i}}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8s+3\\text{i}}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3s+8\\text{i}}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{8s+3\\text{i}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-